        "raw": "<p>Well, *that* was one of the more brutal smackdowns I&#39;ve ever received in SotM.&nbsp; Setup (randomized) was Bunker, Tachyon, Haka, and Tempest vs Citizen Dawn (advanced) in Megalopolis.<br /><br />As her setup, CD put out Citizen Sweat, Citizen Tears, and Citizen Truth.&nbsp; Her turn 1 play was Blinding Blast.&nbsp; So my heroes took considerably less initial HP damage than typical, but had to discard *ALL* their cards.&nbsp; Plus, The Tears/Sweat combo would keep making us discard 2 more cards every round (if we *had* that many), and Citizen Truth was very effectively protecting that combo.&nbsp; In Round 1, 3 out of my 4 heroes had nothing better to do than draw 2 cards that were doomed to be discarded, whereas Haka got to do a whopping *1* point of damage to Citizen Truth.<br /><br />Things improved ever-so-slightly when a Rooftop Combat came out, allowing Haka to do 2 points a round to Truth, and Tempest to do 1.&nbsp; Still, it was literally round 7 before I got a chance to play *any* cards, having been forced to discard a collective *56* cards up to that point!&nbsp; By then my team&#39;s HP were at 4/1/2/0, and it&#39;s not like we had *good* cards to play, so it was soon over.&nbsp; Over the course of the whole game, CD did far more damage to *herself* (via Channel the Eclipse) than I did.<br /><br />Amusingly, in the rematch (still in progress), CD had almost the oposite setup: no control cards to speak of, but tons of raw damage: Assault, Battery, Hammer, and Anvil.&nbsp; I&#39;m two heroes down in that game, but we have a decent chance at least...</p>",
